---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../styles/packmetry-workspace.css';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Packmetry Privacy — How the current browser-first product handles data"
  description="Packmetry's current privacy approach: browser-local workspace data, email contact, technical hosting data and the boundaries of the current product."
>
  <main class="pm-privacy">
    <header class="pm-privacy-hero">
      <p class="pm-privacy-eyebrow">
        Privacy
      </p>

      <h1>
        Privacy,
        <span>explained plainly.</span>
      </h1>

      <p>
        Packmetry is currently designed as a
        browser-first workbench. This page explains
        what stays in your browser, what you may
        choose to send to Packmetry, and where
        third-party infrastructure can still be
        involved.
      </p>

      <p class="pm-privacy-updated">
        Last updated: 6 October 2026
      </p>
    </header>

    <section
      class="pm-privacy-summary"
      aria-labelledby="privacy-summary-title"
    >
      <div>
        <p class="pm-privacy-eyebrow">
          At a glance
        </p>

        <h2 id="privacy-summary-title">
          The current product keeps the core
          packing workflow local.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="pm-privacy-summary-points">
        <article>
          <span aria-hidden="true">01</span>

          <div>
            <strong>
              Workspace data is browser-local
            </strong>

            <p>
              Recent items, plans, saved cartons,
              projects and preferences are stored
              in your browser in the current
              product.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article>
          <span aria-hidden="true">02</span>

          <div>
            <strong>
              No account is required
            </strong>

            <p>
              Packmetry does not currently require
              a user account or cloud workspace to
              run the Personal or Business packing
              tools.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article>
          <span aria-hidden="true">03</span>

          <div>
            <strong>
              Email is user-initiated
            </strong>

            <p>
              Information reaches Packmetry
              directly when you choose to send an
              email or otherwise provide it.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pm-privacy-policy">
      <aside class="pm-privacy-index">
        <p class="pm-privacy-eyebrow">
          Current policy
        </p>

        <nav aria-label="Privacy policy sections">
          <a href="#browser-local">
            Browser-local data
          </a>

          <a href="#contact-data">
            Information you send
          </a>

          <a href="#technical-data">
            Technical data
          </a>

          <a href="#tracking">
            Cookies &amp; analytics
          </a>

          <a href="#control">
            Your control
          </a>

          <a href="#changes">
            Future changes
          </a>
        </nav>
      </aside>

      <div class="pm-privacy-prose">
        <section id="browser-local">
          <p class="pm-privacy-section-number">
            01
          </p>

          <h2>Browser-local workspace data</h2>

          <p>
            The current Packmetry application uses
            browser storage to keep parts of your
            workspace available between visits.
            Depending on the feature, this includes
            technologies such as
            <strong>IndexedDB</strong> and
            <strong>localStorage</strong>.
          </p>

          <p>
            Examples include recent Personal items
            and packing plans, unit preferences,
            saved Business cartons, recent Business
            projects, and selected handling or
            optimization preferences.
          </p>

          <p>
            This data is stored on the device and
            browser profile where you use
            Packmetry. The current product does not
            require that workspace data to be
            uploaded to a Packmetry account or
            cloud workspace.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="contact-data">
          <p class="pm-privacy-section-number">
            02
          </p>

          <h2>Information you choose to send</h2>

          <p>
            If you email
            <a href="mailto:packmetry@gmail.com">
              packmetry@gmail.com
            </a>,
            Packmetry may receive the information
            included in your message, such as your
            email address, message text,
            attachments and ordinary email
            metadata.
          </p>

          <p>
            That information may be retained as
            reasonably necessary to respond,
            understand feedback, investigate a
            reported issue, or maintain relevant
            correspondence.
          </p>

          <div class="pm-privacy-note">
            <strong>
              Please avoid sensitive information
            </strong>

            <p>
              Do not send passwords, payment card
              details, authentication secrets or
              other information that is not needed
              to explain your question or issue.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="technical-data">
          <p class="pm-privacy-section-number">
            03
          </p>

          <h2>Technical and hosting data</h2>

          <p>
            Even when application workspace data
            stays in your browser, the services
            used to host and deliver a website may
            process standard technical request
            information.
          </p>

          <p>
            Depending on the hosting or network
            provider, this can include information
            such as an IP address, browser or
            user-agent information, requested URLs,
            request times, and security or error
            logs. Those infrastructure practices
            are separate from Packmetry's
            browser-local workspace storage.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="tracking">
          <p class="pm-privacy-section-number">
            04
          </p>

          <h2>Cookies, analytics and advertising</h2>

          <p>
            At the time of this policy, the current
            Packmetry application code does not
            include advertising trackers or
            analytics trackers, and Packmetry does
            not use application-set advertising
            cookies.
          </p>

          <p>
            If analytics, advertising, cloud
            accounts or similar services are added
            later, this policy should be updated to
            explain what is collected and why.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="control">
          <p class="pm-privacy-section-number">
            05
          </p>

          <h2>Your control over current data</h2>

          <p>
            Browser-local Packmetry data is tied to
            your browser storage. You can remove
            local data using your browser's site
            data or storage controls. Clearing that
            data can also remove recent work,
            preferences, saved cartons or projects
            stored only in that browser.
          </p>

          <p>
            Business project JSON exports are files
            you control directly. If you export,
            copy or share one of those files, its
            handling depends on where you save or
            send it.
          </p>

          <p>
            For personal information that you sent
            directly to Packmetry by email, you can
            contact
            <a href="mailto:packmetry@gmail.com">
              packmetry@gmail.com
            </a>
            with a privacy-related request.
            Applicable legal or operational
            retention requirements may still
            apply.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="changes">
          <p class="pm-privacy-section-number">
            06
          </p>

          <h2>Future product changes</h2>

          <p>
            Packmetry is still expanding. Future
            versions may add accounts, cloud
            storage, integrations, APIs, analytics
            or other services that change how data
            is handled.
          </p>

          <p>
            When a material change affects privacy,
            this page should be updated so the
            published policy matches the product
            that users actually receive.
          </p>

          <p>
            Questions about this policy can be sent
            to
            <a href="mailto:packmetry@gmail.com">
              packmetry@gmail.com
            </a>.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .pm-privacy {
    width: min(
      calc(100% - 40px),
      1240px
    );
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 82px 0 84px;
  }

  .pm-privacy-eyebrow {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--pm-forest);
    font-size: 0.71rem;
    font-weight: 740;
    letter-spacing: 0.09em;
    line-height: 1.3;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .pm-privacy-hero {
    max-width: 900px;
    padding-bottom: 70px;
  }

  .pm-privacy-hero h1 {
    margin: 18px 0 0;
    color: var(--pm-ink-strong);
    font-size: clamp(
      3.2rem,
      6vw,
      5.8rem
    );
    font-weight: 680;
    letter-spacing: -0.062em;
    line-height: 0.94;
  }

  .pm-privacy-hero h1 span {
    display: block;
    color: #556165;
    font-weight: 560;
  }

  .pm-privacy-hero > p:not(
    .pm-privacy-eyebrow,
    .pm-privacy-updated
  ) {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 27px 0 0;
    color: var(--pm-ink-soft);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .pm-privacy-updated {
    margin: 22px 0 0;
    color: #7c8588;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 610;
  }

  .pm-privacy-summary {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns:
      minmax(0, 0.9fr)
      minmax(0, 1.1fr);
    gap: clamp(
      46px,
      7vw,
      88px
    );
    align-items: start;
    border: 1px solid #dbe2df;
    border-radius: 14px;
    padding:
      clamp(32px, 5vw, 56px);
    background:
      linear-gradient(
        135deg,
        #f3f7f5 0%,
        #f8faf9 100%
      );
  }

  .pm-privacy-summary h2 {
    max-width: 500px;
    margin: 12px 0 0;
    color: var(--pm-ink-strong);
    font-size: clamp(
      1.9rem,
      3.4vw,
      3rem
    );
    font-weight: 640;
    letter-spacing: -0.045em;
    line-height: 1.05;
  }

  .pm-privacy-summary-points {
    border-top: 1px solid #d8e1de;
  }

  .pm-privacy-summary-points article {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns:
      34px
      minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 16px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #d8e1de;
    padding: 18px 0;
  }

  .pm-privacy-summary-points article > span {
    color: #93a09c;
    font-size: 0.67rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .pm-privacy-summary-points strong {
    color: var(--pm-ink-strong);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .pm-privacy-summary-points p {
    margin: 6px 0 0;
    color: var(--pm-ink-soft);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .pm-privacy-policy {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns:
      230px
      minmax(0, 760px);
    gap: clamp(
      60px,
      10vw,
      130px
    );
    margin-top: 78px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--pm-line);
    padding-top: 62px;
  }

  .pm-privacy-index {
    align-self: start;
    position: sticky;
    top: 28px;
  }

  .pm-privacy-index nav {
    display: grid;
    margin-top: 18px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--pm-line);
  }

  .pm-privacy-index a {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--pm-line);
    padding: 11px 0;
    color: var(--pm-ink-soft);
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    font-weight: 640;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .pm-privacy-index a:hover {
    color: var(--pm-forest);
  }

  .pm-privacy-prose > section {
    scroll-margin-top: 30px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--pm-line);
    padding: 0 0 46px;
    margin-bottom: 46px;
  }

  .pm-privacy-prose > section:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .pm-privacy-section-number {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    color: var(--pm-forest);
    font-size: 0.67rem;
    font-weight: 740;
    letter-spacing: 0.07em;
  }

  .pm-privacy-prose h2 {
    margin: 0 0 18px;
    color: var(--pm-ink-strong);
    font-size: clamp(
      1.55rem,
      2.5vw,
      2.15rem
    );
    font-weight: 660;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  .pm-privacy-prose p {
    margin: 0 0 18px;
    color: #465055;
    font-size: 0.94rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .pm-privacy-prose p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .pm-privacy-prose strong {
    color: var(--pm-ink-strong);
    font-weight: 690;
  }

  .pm-privacy-prose a {
    color: var(--pm-forest);
    font-weight: 650;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .pm-privacy-note {
    margin: 30px 0;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--pm-forest);
    padding: 4px 0 4px 17px;
  }

  .pm-privacy-note strong {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 5px;
    color: var(--pm-forest);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.045em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .pm-privacy-note p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--pm-ink-soft);
    font-size: 0.84rem;
    line-height: 1.62;
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .pm-privacy {
      width: calc(100% - 32px);
      padding: 48px 0 56px;
    }

    .pm-privacy-hero {
      padding-bottom: 50px;
    }

    .pm-privacy-hero h1 {
      font-size: clamp(
        2.8rem,
        14vw,
        4rem
      );
    }

    .pm-privacy-summary {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 28px;
      padding: 26px 22px;
    }

    .pm-privacy-policy {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 38px;
      margin-top: 54px;
      padding-top: 44px;
    }

    .pm-privacy-index {
      position: static;
    }

    .pm-privacy-index nav {
      grid-template-columns:
        repeat(
          2,
          minmax(0, 1fr)
        );
    }

    .pm-privacy-index a {
      padding-right: 12px;
    }

    .pm-privacy-prose > section {
      padding-bottom: 38px;
      margin-bottom: 38px;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 359px) {
    .pm-privacy-index nav {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
